<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
    Phase 787 — the boundary that stops the repository-wide MSBuild walk at
    the generated oracle.

    **It deliberately does NOT import the parent.** MSBuild walks up from a
    project directory until it finds a `Directory.Build.props` and stops
    there unless that file imports its own parent; this one does not, so
    the repo-root props never reaches `RemotingDecode.fs`. That is the same
    structural mechanism `templates/safer/` and
    `templates/platformsdk-solution/` use, and the exemption is mirrored in
    the root props' documented NOT-COVERED list and in
    `ArchitectureFitness.fs0025ExemptPrefixes` — a test asserts the two
    agree, so this cannot be widened without saying so where authors read
    the policy.

    WHY IT IS NEEDED. `RemotingDecode.fs` is emitted by the F* extractor,
    which generates one field projector per constructor argument. Each
    extracts as a single-case `match` over the nine-case value union — an
    FS0025 incomplete-match warning apiece, seventeen in all. The root
    props promotes FS0025 to an error tree-wide (Phase 624), and the gate
    that keeps that promotion meaningful pins at ZERO the two ways to
    silence it locally: `#nowarn "25"` in the file, and FS0025 in a
    project's `NoWarn` / `WarningsNotAsErrors`. Both are correct
    prohibitions and neither is the answer here, because the third option
    the gate's message assumes — "fix the matches" — does not exist for a
    file nobody wrote and that a byte-diff holds identical to the
    extractor's output.

    The projectors cannot be suppressed at the source either: F*'s
    `no_auto_projectors` attribute is deprecated and a no-op on the pinned
    release ("projectors are declaration-only; this attribute is a no-op"),
    and the extractor has no flag to omit them. So the honest move is to
    put the generated subtree outside the policy, in the documented way,
    rather than to exempt it quietly inside the policy.

    WHAT IS LOST, so nobody has to re-derive it: the root props sets the
    FS0025 promotion, `GenerateDocumentationFile`, and package metadata
    guarded on `IsPackable != false`. This project is `IsPackable=false`
    and sets its own doc-file property, so nothing else here is affected.
    A project added under `proofs/oracle/` in future inherits this file
    rather than the root one — which is why nothing but the generated
    oracle should live here.
-->
<Project>
</Project>
